\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Cross-lingual knowledge conflict in multilingual LLMs. When a context passage contradicts the model's parametric knowledge, the language of presentation (English vs.\ Chinese) can bias the answer toward different sources. We ask three questions: (1)~Is the conflict signal linearly detectable in the residual stream? (2)~Do probes transfer across languages, and is the transfer symmetric? (3)~Does detection imply causal influence on resolution?}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:hero}{{1}{2}{Cross-lingual knowledge conflict in multilingual LLMs. When a context passage contradicts the model's parametric knowledge, the language of presentation (English vs.\ Chinese) can bias the answer toward different sources. We ask three questions: (1)~Is the conflict signal linearly detectable in the residual stream? (2)~Do probes transfer across languages, and is the transfer symmetric? (3)~Does detection imply causal influence on resolution?}{figure.caption.1}{}}
