\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Transfer asymmetry ($\Delta _{\text  {asym}}$) with bootstrap 95\% CIs ($n = 2{,}000$) for conflict and XNLI tasks across all three architectures (six data points). Conflict and XNLI CIs overlap substantially within each model, indicating that the ZH$\to $EN advantage is a general cross-lingual property rather than conflict-specific. Grey dashed lines: $\pm $2~pp exploratory equivalence margin (TOST power $= 1.4$\%; see \S  \ref {sec:xnli_baseline}).}}{6}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:asymmetry_forest}{{4}{6}{Transfer asymmetry ($\Delta _{\text {asym}}$) with bootstrap 95\% CIs ($n = 2{,}000$) for conflict and XNLI tasks across all three architectures (six data points). Conflict and XNLI CIs overlap substantially within each model, indicating that the ZH$\to $EN advantage is a general cross-lingual property rather than conflict-specific. Grey dashed lines: $\pm $2~pp exploratory equivalence margin (TOST power $= 1.4$\%; see \S \ref {sec:xnli_baseline})}{figure.caption.12}{}}
