\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Detection--decision dissociation across three architectures. For Llama, the linear probe peak (L15, 47\% depth), MLP probe peak (L18, 56\%), and causal steering node (L13, 41\%) cluster in mid-layers; upper layers (e.g., L28) retain detectable signal but lack causal influence. Qwen and Gemma achieve comparable probe accuracy but show no significant causal site under linear steering, illustrating that detectability does not imply causal relevance.}}{11}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dissociation}{{6}{11}{Detection--decision dissociation across three architectures. For Llama, the linear probe peak (L15, 47\% depth), MLP probe peak (L18, 56\%), and causal steering node (L13, 41\%) cluster in mid-layers; upper layers (e.g., L28) retain detectable signal but lack causal influence. Qwen and Gemma achieve comparable probe accuracy but show no significant causal site under linear steering, illustrating that detectability does not imply causal relevance}{figure.caption.27}{}}
